# One file, two build contexts: the devcontainer image (its Dockerfile uses `..`
# as the context, and Compose mounts the repo rather than copying it) and the VPS
# fallback image at the root, which *does* copy the checkout. Secrets,
# dependencies and local data stay out of both (PLAN §14.4).
.git
node_modules
data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
backups
*.log
.pupkeep
.pi
.pi/todos
.devcontainer/.cache
npm-debug.log*

# The app image copies the checkout but needs none of these, and the devcontainer
# reads the repo from its mount rather than from the context.
test
docs
*.md
!README.md
!NOTICE.md
